Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  Bug Hunter — allow web push over plain HTTP on the private VPN
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
;  Service Workers + the Push API only run in a "secure context". A plain-HTTP
;  VPN origin is NOT a secure context, so browsers disable push there. This
;  policy tells Chrome and Edge to treat the listed origin(s) as secure, which
;  re-enables push WITHOUT a certificate. See docs/insecure-origin-push.md.
;
;  HOW TO USE
;    1. Replace the example origin below with YOUR exact VPN origin:
;         scheme + host + port, NO trailing slash, e.g. http://your-vpn-host.example:8765
;       Add "2"=, "3"=, ... for additional origins.
;    2. Apply on each client: double-click this file, or run from an elevated
;       prompt:  reg import scripts\web-push-insecure-origin.reg
;       (or deploy the same keys via Group Policy Preferences across the domain).
;    3. Fully restart the browser. Confirm at chrome://policy / edge://policy
;       that OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin shows your origin.
;
;  NOTE: This is a deliberate security relaxation — only safe because the origin
;  is reachable solely over your trusted private VPN. Never list a public URL.
; ============================================================================

; --- Google Chrome ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin]
"1"="http://your-vpn-host.example:8765"

; --- Microsoft Edge ---
[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\OverrideSecurityRestrictionsOnInsecureOrigin]
"1"="http://your-vpn-host.example:8765"
